.SH NAME
migrable-completion-zsh - Generate the autocompletion script for zsh


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmigrable completion zsh [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate the autocompletion script for the zsh shell.

.PP
If shell completion is not already enabled in your environment you will need
to enable it.  You can execute the following once:

.EX
echo "autoload -U compinit; compinit" >> ~/.zshrc
.EE

.PP
To load completions in your current shell session:

.EX
source <(migrable completion zsh)
.EE

.PP
To load completions for every new session, execute once:

.SS Linux:
.EX
migrable completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_migrable"
.EE

.SS macOS:
.EX
migrable completion zsh > $(brew --prefix)/share/zsh/site-functions/_migrable
.EE

.PP
You will need to start a new shell for this setup to take effect.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for zsh

.PP
\fB--no-descriptions\fP[=false]
	disable completion descriptions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config-dir\fP=""
	path to configuration directory

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	enable verbose output


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmigrable-completion(1)\fP


